><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251113105050+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251113105100+10'00'" name="d0dc2f35-1443-4859-a218-0300bc619c6f" page="9" coords="310.733795,695.799377,362.583191,695.799377,310.733795,683.755859,362.583191,683.755859" rect="310.357422,683.379517,362.959534,696.175720" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: there was no clear practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="609.448975,603.799377,793.448975,695.799377"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251113105108+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="d0dc2f35-1443-4859-a218-0300bc619c6f" date="D:20251113105108+10'00'" name="f77368f2-b144-426d-ac92-5d3eabff588a" icon="Comment" page="9" rect="310.357422,672.175720,334.357422,696.175720" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Taken together, the present study provides valuable scientific&#xD;innovation among monitoring research as well as applied sport&#xD;science. In accordance with the German original, the English&#xD;ARSS and SRSS emerged as two valid and reliable tools which&#xD;were developed on a sound theoretical background and are&#xD;suitable for economical applications in individual as well as&#xD;group settings. The quality criteria of psychometric test construction&#xD;were replicated among a large sample of the target population.&#xD;The unique approach of shortening the ARSS to the SRSS is&#xD;now generalised to a broader athletic population to address the&#xD;necessity of providing short scales to increase athletes’ compliance&#xD;(Horvath &amp; Röthlin, </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#00007F;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2018</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>; Saw et al., </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#00007F;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2017</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>, </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#00007F;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2015a</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). Moreover,&#xD;to the best of our knowledge, this was the first study within sport&#xD;psychology and sport science that explicitly considered different&#xD;English-speaking regions in the validation process and provides&#xD;proof of strong measurement invariance.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="609.448975,604.175720,793.448975,696.175720"
/></text
></annots
><f href="../pdfs/10.1080_02640414.2019.1684790.pdf"
/><ids original="01721B446E2E7A07A95E1895707B2DFE" modified="01721B446E2E7A07A95E1895707B2DFE"
/></xfdf
>